reac-pw (1.0.39) unstable; urgency=medium

  * tests: a bridge enslaving the NIC reads stacked; the guard goes red when
    removed (#46)
  * changelog: the host-NIC rule ships as 1.0.39; 1.0.38 was tagged before it
    (#46)
  * changelog: 1.0.38 names the host-NIC rule (#46) and carries the
    unpublished 1.0.37
  * tests: the held arm reads addr-added from its own transcript, as every
    other mark of the run (#46)
  * tests: a pinned master on a NIC that carries the host's address makes no
    edge, whole binary (#46)
  * knock: a stream rung on the host's NIC goes out as a control knock, both
    ladders read the kernel, the roster counts edges (#46)
  * reac_wake: the host's NIC is a refusal of its own, read before the facts
    about our push (#46)
  * reac_link_owner: the kernel says whether an interface is the host's, from
    three rtnetlink dumps (#46)
  * docs: a NIC the host uses gets no stream knock and no PHY edge (#46)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:10:07 +0000
